  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "A matrix is a rectangular array of numbers; matrices add, multiply, and solve linear systems.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Matrix basics",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Add matrices of the same size entrywise. For a \\( 2\\times2 \\) matrix with rows \\( (a,b) \\) and \\( (c,d) \\), the determinant is \\( ad-bc \\). A system \\( A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b} \\) solves as \\( \\mathbf{x}=A^{-1}\\mathbf{b} \\) when the determinant is non-zero.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Order",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "rows × columns",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Add",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "entrywise",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Determinant",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( ad-bc \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Solve",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\mathbf{x}=A^{-1}\\mathbf{b} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 10.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the determinant of the matrix with rows \\( (2,1) \\) and \\( (3,4) \\).</p>\\[ 2(4)-1(3)=5. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Solving a 3×3 system",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Use the inverse matrix method to solve \\(2x+y=5\\), \\(x-3y=1\\).</p>\\[A=\\begin{pmatrix}2&1\\\\1&-3\\end{pmatrix},\\;\\det A=-6-1=-7,\\;A^{-1}=\\frac{1}{-7}\\begin{pmatrix}-3&-1\\\\-1&2\\end{pmatrix}.\\]\\[\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=A^{-1}\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}=\\frac{1}{-7}\\begin{pmatrix}-16\\\\-3\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}16/7\\\\3/7\\end{pmatrix}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find the value(s) of \\(k\\) for which \\(A=\\begin{pmatrix}k&2\\\\3&k\\end{pmatrix}\\) is singular.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(\\det A=k^2-6=0\\Rightarrow k=\\pm\\sqrt6\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
